id: pm-web-7ppe
title: "View consented agent questions, context receipts and evidence gaps"
description: "Acceptance: a viewer cannot read another scope packet; revoked access invalidates future retrieval; UI and API show identical omission receipts. Provide typed SDK and CLI, bounded TOON/JSON, revision-bound explicit consent, remedies, Triplicate UI, docs and example, synthetic desktop/mobile evidence, public tracker read-only no-git validation, and npm/Bun CI gates. No inference, memory or new backend."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-23T08:14:19.939Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-23T11:43:17.681Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[17]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T08:14:44.443Z",codex-agent,"Overlap check: core SDK owns PmReadOutputSessionReceipt and PmReadOutputReceipt, cross-call accounting, suppression and output rendering. pm-context owns pack assembly and pm-context-usage/v1 receipts. Decision inbox covers Plan decisions, not scoped context. This feature adapts existing receipt metadata and uses the existing pm-web PostgreSQL store, with no inference, memory, or second backend. Scope authorization must be separate from generic tracker reads. Preserve pinned CLI 2026.10.19; no new core lease behavior is needed. Acceptance: deny other-scope packets, invalidate retrieval after revocation, and render identical API omission reasons/remedies in the UI."
  "2026-10-23T08:24:34.564Z",codex-agent,"Implemented scoped receipt metadata in the existing PostgreSQL store, with explicit audience consent, server-derived publisher identity, atomic revision replacement and deletion, and current project access checks. Native commands use authenticated HTTP and core TOON/JSON rendering; SDK adapters consume core output-session and pm-context public receipts. Six targeted real HTTP/SDK/native CLI regressions passed, including a no-git tracker with no git executable. Targeted new-server coverage: 100 percent statements, lines and functions; 89.74 percent branches. Synthetic browser acceptance passed at 1440 and 390 pixels: two receipt omissions and one gap match API text exactly, no horizontal overflow, and refreshing after revocation removes the question. Public validation: public main a11f58c, 176 certified items, 383 immutable source files, 11 returned bounded rows, 3 suppressed repeats, 1541 estimated source tokens within 1600, two receipt omissions, one gap, 660 packet JSON bytes, source hashes unchanged. Full npm and Bun release gates will run in CI to avoid saturating the shared host."
  "2026-10-23T08:24:58.426Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: changing only AgentContextClient.publish back to the unfiltered binding spread made the audience-removal regression fail (one selected test failed). Changing only getAgentContext to omit its audience predicate made the cross-scope regression fail (one selected test failed). Each control restored the exact original source bytes; these are semantic guard regressions, with no fixture or assertion edits. Receipt assertion boundaries and revocation limitations are documented in docs/agent-context.md."
  "2026-10-23T08:25:56.553Z",codex-agent,"Final public-copy rerun after sharing the read-only extraction helper: 176 items, 383 source files unchanged, 11 output rows, 3 suppressed repeats, 1542 source estimated tokens within the 1600 ceiling, 660 packet JSON bytes and 2182 ms measured. Source hash b9804cb4006952199fb8b26b4d98a0804b9cfd4e013bcdbda73ee5f8e6ce7ae9. Core receipt token estimates include clock-bearing metadata and can vary slightly between reads. The decision-inbox public-data validator also passed after reuse of the helper."
  "2026-10-23T08:27:06.564Z",codex-agent,The linked pm test command passed all six regressions (zero failures/skips). Both behavioral negative controls failed the intended selected test and restored exact source bytes. Targeted schema compatibility checks passed two source/built doctor journeys; schema revision 2 adds only the context metadata table and index in the existing database. CI also replays synthetic browser acceptance on Node 26. Claims will be released with the review-ready PR; the item remains in progress for orchestrator verification.
  "2026-10-23T08:30:54.365Z",codex-agent,"Final transport review added two concrete remedies: SDK network or malformed-response failures normalize to typed unavailable refusals; a queued offline revocation tells the publisher that access remains active until server confirmation. Added a real refused-loopback connection regression and native host missing-configuration refusal. Reclaimed the item for this small follow-up; full CI evidence will use the final commit."
  "2026-10-23T08:32:12.516Z",codex-agent,"Final transport acceptance passed: seven real SDK/HTTP/native regressions, plus synthetic browser checks that queued revocation keeps the question visible and access active until a real server revocation, after which viewer refresh clears the packet. All existing scope and revision acceptance still passes. Source/built doctor tests passed 2 of 2; schema-version tests passed 3 of 3; extension registration passed 1 of 1."
  "2026-10-23T08:34:07.918Z",codex-agent,"Committed the final real-data measurement as docs/agent-context-validation.json. The receipt projection now uses the actual serving timestamp instead of a fixed measurement timestamp: 176 public items, 383 immutable source files unchanged, 11 rows, 3 suppressed repeats, 1542 source tokens within 1600, two omission reasons, one gap, 664 packet JSON bytes, 925 ms measured. This report supersedes the earlier 660-byte fixed-timestamp projection; public source SHA and source hash are unchanged."
  "2026-10-23T08:54:07.717Z",codex-agent,"Tightened the agent refusal contract: unavailable HTTP/network dependencies now use core EXIT_CODE.DEPENDENCY_FAILED in the CLI, matching the existing inbox convention, instead of being classified as usage errors. The real refused-connection regression now asserts this exact core exit code as well as the typed SDK remedy. Seven targeted regressions pass with this mapping."
  "2026-10-23T09:40:07.760Z",codex-agent,"Review follow-up: fix both blockers without hosted access. Open packet views must clear after audience removal, project-share revocation, or packet deletion through realtime invalidation plus bounded disconnected fallback checks. Keyed responses must recheck current route authorization and stored resource visibility at the common idempotency boundary, with an audit of every covered mutation family and regressions for context plus another route. Refresh Triplicate screenshots after sidebar and spacing fixes; record semantic revert proofs and await npm/Bun CI gates."
  "2026-10-23T10:09:51.676Z",codex-agent,"Implemented the shared replay authorizer with an explicit 78-route inventory and drift regression. Every replay checks current principal/resource authority and never reexecutes the mutation. Opaque provider/extension-command/graph-query/presence responses fail closed with live-read remedies. Packet replay requires current project capability, publisher, audience and exact revision. Realtime content-free invalidation covers packet writes/deletion, direct/group project sharing, membership changes and account/project removal. Revoked project streams send a terminal access-revoked control frame before closing. Open views clear on signals, use a serialized ten-second fallback with a five-second read deadline, clear hidden-tab content and guard late responses. Targeted 106-test run passed; changed replay/access coverage measured 97.39 percent statements and lines, 83.33 percent branches, 100 percent functions. Both refreshed Triplicate screenshots were visually checked for the three requested nits. Six open-session browser revocations passed: audience, sharing and deletion, each through SSE and disconnected fallback."
  "2026-10-23T10:13:38.999Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs (assertions/fixtures unchanged): removing only finishSettled's replay authorization block made both selected real-HTTP regressions fail (0 pass, 2 fail): context replay returned cached 201 instead of 404 after revision replacement, and PM create replay returned cached 201 instead of 403 after editor downgrade. Command: node scripts/with-test-db.ts node --test --test-name-pattern='keyed context publish cannot resurrect|another idempotent PM route refuses' test/idempotency-access.test.ts. Replacing only the view's invalidateAgentContext, revokeAgentContextView and scheduleValidation bodies with their previous no-op behavior, then rebuilding frontend, caused the unchanged local-server browser regression to fail waiting three seconds for the revoked state after deletion in an already open view. Exact source bytes were restored and frontend rebuilt. Positive restored runs cover all six SSE/disconnected audience/share/delete cases. Linked pm tests ran successfully: 7 plus 44 tests, 51 executions, no skips; project test-result tracking is disabled, so this comment preserves results without changing tracker configuration."
  "2026-10-23T10:13:49.406Z",codex-agent,"Restored positive verification completed: all six automatic open-session revocations passed with no manual refresh, matching omission/gap text at 1440px and 390px and no horizontal overflow; screenshots refreshed. Current typecheck, test typecheck, lint, zero-clone duplication and docstring gate (854 declarations) pass. Main was merged without tracker conflicts. Full unchanged-threshold npm and Bun release checks are delegated to the PR CI matrix; results will be linked in the PR body. No hosted folders or services were accessed. No pm CLI/SDK defect was encountered; the existing disabled test-result tracking setting was preserved."
  "2026-10-23T10:16:53.348Z",codex-agent,"Main advanced while CI was queued with the version-only 2026.10.23 release. Integrated that upstream release so final gate evidence covers the current base; package version, manifest, generated entrypoint and release changelog stay aligned. No feature or dependency behavior changed. Previous targeted results and behavioral revert proofs remain valid; CI will verify the merged head."
  "2026-10-23T10:36:28.567Z",codex-agent,"First full CI exposed ten legacy fixture failures out of 805 tests (795 passed, no skips), with source coverage above unchanged thresholds. Updated the extracted SSE callback realm to supply and assert context invalidation; fanout tests now assert only the literal content-free terminal control frame follows prior authorized frames and no private data leaks; the custom account-only worker probe now explicitly reauthorizes its current database account on replay. Production code and behavioral revert proofs are unchanged. The affected 36 tests pass; test typecheck, lint, zero-clone duplication and docstrings pass. Superseded CI was canceled so the corrected fixture head can run the complete npm/Bun matrix."
  "2026-10-23T11:18:35.595Z",codex-agent,"All four npm/Bun release gates passed on the prior head (805 tests, 2 capacity tests and 4 packed scenarios per gate, zero failures/skips), including all six browser revocations. Final check review separately found CodeQL's security result was failing despite its workflow job succeeding: the deliberately unconfigured embedding probe in test/idempotency-access.test.ts lacked a write limiter. Added the existing createTierLimiters write tier before the fixture guard, matching production order; no production behavior changed and no alert was dismissed. Targeted replay regressions and test typecheck/lint pass. Rerunning all final-head checks after this fixture security correction."
  "2026-10-23T11:43:16.696Z",codex-agent,"Final-head Node 26 passed both npm/Bun gates and all six browser revocations; Node 22 npm passed, but its Bun suite exposed one existing asynchronous settlement race (804/805 passed). The concurrent-writer test asserted ledger completion immediately after HTTP/SSE completion, when both SQL outcomes were still pending. Added a bounded three-second poll of actual ledger status before the unchanged exact status, principal, history-integrity and SSE assertions. No production behavior, thresholds or skips changed. All nine PM command access tests pass; test typecheck, lint and zero-clone duplication pass. All four linked pm test commands pass (7 + 44 + 36 + 9 = 96 test executions). CodeQL's separate security check passed after the rate-limited probe correction. Original finding revert proofs remain valid because their production functions and assertions are unchanged."
